    "https://www.keystone.edu/2026/07/29/head-mens-volleyball-coach-sports-information-assistant/": {
      "title": "Head Men’s Volleyball Coach / Sports Information Assistant",
      "description": "Head Men's Volleyball Coach / Sports Information Assistant - Keystone College 1-800-824-2764 admissions@keystone.edu Calendar Directory QUICK LINKS Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Resident Dining Current Students Faculty & Staff Library News Visiting Give Now How to Apply About Keystone Accreditations and Authorizations Campus & La Plume Community College Publications and Media History of Keystone Mission, Vision, Strategic Plan Office of the President Student Consumer Information Your Community Partner Departments and Office Hours Admissions Visit Why Choose Keystone? Undergraduate International Students Tuition and Aid Accepted Students Parents Veteran and Military Students Academics Majors, Minors Online Programs Graduate Programs Schools and Programs Career Development Student Success Center Meet Our Faculty Registrar Study Abroad Dual Enrollment/High School Programs Apprenticeship Programs Honors Program Undergraduate Research Continuing Education Online Degree Programs Professional Development Programs (Online) Customized Workforce Training Credit Certificates and Workforce Education Self-Paced Courses and Certificates Personal Enrichment Certificates and Credentials for Educators Community and Recreation Programs KCEEI – Keystone College Environmental Education Institute KC3D Campus Life Activities and Events for Students Campus Resources for Support and Success Dining Belong at Keystone Title IX Policy and Procedures Keystone KeyKard Living on Campus Visiting Campus Alumni Alumni Events, Reunions and Visits Alumni Benefits Our Alumni Get Involved Alumni Oral History Project Giving How to Give Donor Recognition Impact of Giving Naming Opportunities Athletics Select Page APPLY NOW + Home » Job Posting - Professional Staff » Head Men’s Volleyball Coach / Sports Information Assistant Head Men’s Volleyball Coach / Sports Information Assistant Jul 29, 2026 | Job Posting - Professional Staff DEPARTMENT: Athletics; Contact Kacy Manning; Email kacy.manning@keystone.edu JOB PURPOSE : The Head Men’s Volleyball Coach / Sports Information Assistant is responsible for providing leadership, direction, and coaching expertise to student-athletes within the men’s volleyball program while assisting with athletic communications and sports information operations. This position involves overseeing all aspects of the men’s volleyball program, including recruiting, player development, and program administration, while supporting the promotion of Keystone Athletics through game coverage, statistics, website updates, and media relations. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Develop and implement effective coaching strategies to enhance the performance and skill development of student-athletes in men’s volleyball. Recruit, retain, and motivate talented student-athletes for the men’s volleyball program. Plan and execute comprehensive practice sessions emphasizing skill development, physical conditioning, and teamwork. Plan and coordinate team travel, competitions, recruiting, and other logistical aspects of the program. Provide guidance and support to student-athletes in their academic and personal development while fostering a positive team culture. Collaborate with the athletic department on fundraising initiatives, community engagement, and admissions events. Serve as the Sports Information contact for assigned sports by maintaining statistics, writing game recaps, updating the athletics website, and assisting with social media and promotional efforts. Assist with game management, live statistics, photography, livestreams, and other athletic communications responsibilities. Site supervision and administrative duties as assigned. Comply with all NCAA, conference, and institutional policies and procedures. Promote the volleyball program and Keystone Athletics through community outreach and public relations activities. Stay informed about current trends and advancements in volleyball coaching and athletic communications. Other duties as assigned. SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Familiarity with NCAA rules and regulations. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to organize multiple projects and meet deadlines. Experience with athletics statistics software, website management, social media, and Microsoft Office is preferred. Availability for evening, weekend, and overnight work and travel as required. EXPERIENCE: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. Previous collegiate coaching experience or equivalent preferred. Experience in sports information, athletic communications, media relations, or related field preferred. Commitment to the academic success and personal development of student-athletes. Strong understanding of the technical aspects of men’s volleyball. Knowledge of and adherence to NCAA or other governing body rules and regulations. TO APPLY: Please send resume, cover letter, and names, addresses & phone numbers of three professional references to:  Human Resources * Keystone College * One College Green * La Plume, PA 18440-1099 * email:  humanresources@keystone.edu News by Category Academic News Alumni News Campus News Event News Faculty/Staff Featured News In the News Student News Veteran News News Archives 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 Founded in 1868 and accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education. Maps and Directions. Office Hours: Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. One College Green P.O. Box 50 La Plume, PA 18440-0200 1-800-824-2764 or 570-945-8000 Apply Visit Campus Need help? Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Careers at Keystone College Current Students & Staff Departments and Office Hours Library Student Consumer Information Web Content Policy Web Accessibility Statement Web Disclaimer and Privacy Statement"
    },
