e Office of Student & Residence Life in all facets of the program, specifically within Residence Life and Student Activities. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES • Assist in supervising RAs and hold them accountable for agreed upon hall and departmental expectations. • Ensure students are compliant with the Residence Life and Keystone College policies • Develop and maintain positive relationships with both residents and student staff which promote ongoing communication, mutual support and respect • Assist with RA selection and training • Participate in evening and weekend duty coverage. • Assist the Student Activities Office and student staff with programming Other duties as assigned. SKILLS AND ABILITIES: • On-campus living required; must be available to work flexible hours including evenings, weekends, on-call. • Valid driver’s license & ability to meet requirements to drive College vehicles. • Demonstrated organizational skills and good communication EXPERIENCE: • Bachelor’s degree required. • Experience as a resident assistant preferred. • Acceptance into Keystone’s Graduate program. TO APPLY: Please send resume, cover letter, and names, addresses & phone numbers of three professional references to: Human Resources * Keystone College * One College Green * La Plume, PA 18440-1099 * email: humanresources@keystone.edu News by Category Academic News Alumni News Campus News Event News Faculty/Staff Featured News In the News Student News Veteran News News Archives 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 Founded in 1868 and accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education. Maps and Directions. Office Hours: Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. One College Green P.O. Box 50 La Plume, PA 18440-0200 1-800-824-2764 or 570-945-8000 Apply Visit Campus Need help? Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Careers at Keystone College Current Students & Staff Departments and Office Hours Library Student Consumer Information Web Content Policy Web Accessibility Statement Web Disclaimer an