    "https://www.keystone.edu/2025/04/10/assistant-professor-of-counseling-tenure-track-2/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Counseling (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Counseling (Tenure-Track) - Keystone College 1-800-824-2764 admissions@keystone.edu Calendar Directory QUICK LINKS Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Resident Dining Current Students Faculty & Staff Library News Visiting Give Now How to Apply About Keystone Accreditations and Authorizations Campus & La Plume Community College Publications and Media History of Keystone Mission, Vision, Strategic Plan Office of the President Student Consumer Information Your Community Partner Departments and Office Hours Admissions Visit Why Choose Keystone? Undergraduate International Students Tuition and Aid Accepted Students Parents Veteran and Military Students Academics Majors, Minors Online Programs Graduate Programs Schools and Programs Career Development Student Success Center Meet Our Faculty Registrar Study Abroad Dual Enrollment/High School Programs Apprenticeship Programs Honors Program Undergraduate Research Continuing Education Online Degree Programs Professional Development Programs (Online) Customized Workforce Training Credit Certificates and Workforce Education Self-Paced Courses and Certificates Personal Enrichment Certificates and Credentials for Educators Community and Recreation Programs KCEEI – Keystone College Environmental Education Institute KC3D Campus Life Activities and Events for Students Campus Resources for Support and Success Dining Belong at Keystone Title IX Policy and Procedures Keystone KeyKard Living on Campus Visiting Campus Alumni Alumni Events, Reunions and Visits Alumni Benefits Our Alumni Get Involved Alumni Oral History Project Giving How to Give Donor Recognition Impact of Giving Naming Opportunities Athletics Select Page APPLY NOW + Home » Job Posting - Faculty » Assistant Professor of Counseling (Tenure-Track) Assistant Professor of Counseling (Tenure-Track) Apr 10, 2025 | Job Posting - Faculty Job Title: Assistant Professor of Counseling (Tenure-Track) Location: Keystone College, Social and Behavioral Sciences (SBS) Department, Counseling Program, La Plume, PA Duration: 9-Month Contract, Full-Time Start Date: Fall 2025; may be eligible for January 2025 start. Job Description: The Social and Behavioral Sciences Department at Keystone College in La Plume, PA invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. Candidate must be a licensed professional counselor (LPC) in the state of Pennsylvania (or license eligible). We are seeking a dynamic and dedicated individual who will contribute to the College’s teaching, program development, research, and service missions. This position offers an excellent opportunity for a passionate educator to impact our unique student population and to shape the future of our programs. Responsibilities: 1. Teach graduate and potentially undergraduate courses in psychology and counseling theories, consistent with the applicant’s areas of expertise and the department’s curricular needs. 2. Conduct and publish high-quality, original research in counseling psychology and related fields, with a focus on at least one of the following areas: rural mental health and/or the practice of counseling with culturally diverse populations. 3. Supervise student research projects at both the graduate and undergraduate level. 4. Engage in service activities such as committee participation, program development, and community engagement. 5. Contribute to the development and improvement of the department’s curriculum and programs. 6. Mentor students and provide advising on academic and career-related matters. 7. Actively participate in departmental meetings, Faculty Senate (with committee involvement), faculty development opportunities, and other departmental activities. 8. Engage in interdisciplinary collaboration within and outside the college. 9. Participate in regional and national professional organizations in counseling. 10. Provide clinical supervision to graduate students. Qualifications: 1. Doctoral degree in Counseling/Counselor Education, or related field, from an CACREP-accredited program. 2. Candidate must be licensed, or license-eligible, as a Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) in the state of Pennsylvania 3. Demonstrated ability to teach a diverse range of courses within psychology and counseling fields. 4. Proven track record of research in one or more of the following areas: rural mental health, community counseling, counseling diverse populations, sports psychology, and/or health psychology. 5. Strong commitment to mentorship, student success, and fostering an inclusive learning environment. 6. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. 7. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and the broader local community. TO APPLY: Please send resume, cover letter, and names, addresses & phone numbers of three professional references to: Human Resources * Keystone College * One College Green * La Plume, PA 18440-1099 * email: humanresources@keystone.edu Please also include the following: Upload the following documents: a. Cover letter detailing qualifications, teaching experience, and research interests b. Curriculum vitae (CV). c. Statement of teaching philosophy. d. Statement of research interests. e. Three professional references with contact information. f. Sample publications or research manuscripts (if available). Keystone College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from candidates of all backgrounds. Review of applications will begin as soon as received and continue until the position is filled. We look forward to receiving your application! News by Category Academic News Alumni News Campus News Event News Faculty/Staff Featured News In the News Student News Veteran News News Archives 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 Founded in 1868 and accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education. Maps and Directions. Office Hours: Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. One College Green P.O. Box 50 La Plume, PA 18440-0200 1-800-824-2764 or 570-945-8000 Apply Visit Campus Need help? Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Careers at Keystone College Current Students & Staff Departments and Office Hours Library Student Consumer Information Web Content Policy Web Accessibility Statement Web Disclaimer and Privacy Statement"
    },
