ns of a group of children, creating a warm, loving and nurturing environment encouraging them to learn, develop and advance Ensures constant focus on the well-being, health and safety of children Cleans and sanitizes equipment and toys on a daily basis in accordance with hygiene procedures and participates in the maintenance and necessary housekeeping duties of the classroom, playgrounds and common use areas Helps to maintain an attractive, fun, clean, interactive, and orderly classroom that encourages children to create, play, learn and explore Conducts daily health checks on each child Follows policies and procedures regarding medical and dental emergencies, short-term exclusion of children, and the handling and storing of medication Cultivates positive relationships with children, families, parents, staff, state licensing authorities, volunteers and other stakeholders Contributes to the effective operation of the overall Oppenheim Family Children’s Center Attends all required staff meetings, workshops and/or school functions Participates in the Children’s Center fundraising efforts and events Complies with all rules, regulations, procedures and protocols of the Children’s Center and the local, state or national regulatory agencies pertaining to the health, safety, emergency procedures and care of children Maintains overall professional personal appearance Other duties as required ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Performs other related duties as assigned by supervisor QUALIFICATIONS Experience, Competencies, and Education Bachelor’s Degree in Early Childhood Education PA Early Childhood Education Teaching Certification preferred Minimum of two years’ experience working with young children in an educational setting Background check clearances including Act 34, Act 114, Act 151 and National Sex Offender (NSOR) , names and address of three professional references, two written references, and physical examination with a TB test is required. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Must possess or immediately obtain certification in Pediatric First Aid and CPR Must be able to supervise children by sight and sound at all times Must be physically able to participate with children in a wide variety of indoor and outdoor activities and be able to lift children and move classroom equipment Must complete 24 hours professional development per year Must be able to work a flexible schedule TO APPLY: Please send resume, cover letter and names, addresses & phone numbers of three professional references to:  Human Resources *Keystone College* One College Green * La Plume, PA  18440-1099 * email: humanresources@keystone.edu News by Category Academic News Alumni News Campus News Event News Faculty/Staff Featured News In the News Student News Veteran News News Archives 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 Founded in 1868 and accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education. Maps and Directions. Office Hours: Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. One College Green P.O. Box 50 La Plume, PA 18440-0200 1-800-824-2764 or 570-945-8000 Apply Visit Campus Need help? Bookstore Buy Keystone Gear Careers at Keystone College Current Students & Staff Departments and Office Hours Library Student Consumer Information Web Content Policy Web Accessibility Statement Web Disclaimer and Privacy Statement"
